== Introduction ==

=== Abstract ===  
This proposal extends the Partially Signed Bitcoin Transaction format
(PSBT v2 as defined by BIP-0370) for **Litecoin’s Mimblewimble
Extension-Block (MWEB)** functionality.
It specifies new global, input, output, and *kernel-map* fields that let
wallets collaborate on confidential-amount, signature-aggregated MWEB
transactions while preserving the role-based flow of BIP-0174/BIP-0370.

=== Copyright ===  
This document is licensed under the 2-clause BSD license.

=== Motivation ===  
Litecoin activated MWEB in May 2022 (LTC block 2 249 856), enabling
confidential transfers inside an extension block anchored to each
main-chain block.  
Collaborative transactions—coinjoins, payjoins, multisig, hardware-wallet
workflows—benefit greatly from PSBT.  Without standard key-types
covering MWEB’s **outputs, kernels, offsets, stealth commitments, range
proofs,** etc., wallet interoperability is impossible.  
The goal is **minimal but sufficient** PSBT extensions so that existing
BIP-0370 parsers need only add table entries, not a brand-new format.

== Specification ==

PSBT v2 rules remain unchanged **except** for the additional key-types
tabulated below.  
Field inclusion/exclusion follows BIP-0370 conventions:

* “Versions Requiring Inclusion” — must appear in PSBT v2+MWEB.  
* “Versions Requiring Exclusion” — must **not** appear in PSBT v0.  
* “Versions Allowing Inclusion” — optional.

Where “None” appears under <keydata>, the key consists of the single
<keytype> byte.

