=== Kernel Maps ===

A **kernel map** is encoded exactly like an input/output map but starts
with the separator byte <code>0x00</code> **immediately following the
last output map**.  There MUST be exactly
<tt>PSBT_GLOBAL_MWEB_KERNEL_COUNT</tt> kernel maps.

{| class="wikitable"
! Name 
! <tt><keytype></tt>
! <tt><keydata></tt>
! <tt><valuedata></tt>
! Inc. 
! Exc. 
! Allow
|-
| Excess Commitment || <tt>PSBT_KERN_EXCESS_COMMIT = 0x00</tt> || None || 33-byte commitment || 2 || 0 || 2
|-
| Stealth Excess Commit || <tt>PSBT_KERN_STEALTH_COMMIT = 0x01</tt> || None || 33-byte blinded excess (stealth) ||  || 0 || 2
|-
| Fee (litoshi) || <tt>PSBT_KERN_FEE = 0x02</tt> || None || 64-bit little-endian miner fee inside EB ||  || 0 || 2
|-
| Pegin Amount || <tt>PSBT_KERN_PEGIN_AMOUNT = 0x03</tt> || None || 64-bit little-endian amount coming from main-chain ||  || 0 || 2
|-
| Peg-out TxOut || <tt>PSBT_KERN_PEGOUT = 0x04</tt> || <varint index></varint> || serialized <tt>CTxOut</tt> ||  || 0 || 2
|-
| Lock Height || <tt>PSBT_KERN_LOCK_HEIGHT = 0x05</tt> || None || 32-bit little-endian block-height lock ||  || 0 || 2
|-
| Feature Bits || <tt>PSBT_KERN_FEATURES = 0x06</tt> || None || 1-byte bit-field (see MWEB spec) ||  || 0 || 2
|-
| Extra Data || <tt>PSBT_KERN_EXTRA_DATA = 0x07</tt> || None || opaque bytes committed inside kernel ||  || 0 || 2
|-
| Kernel Signature || <tt>PSBT_KERN_SIG = 0x08</tt> || None || 64-byte Schnorr sig proving excess ownership ||  || 0 || 2
|}

Kernel maps without <tt>Kernel Signature</tt> are **not finalized**.

---

=== Determining the MWEB Offset ===

The **aggregate blinding factor** is computed as  
<code>offset = tx_offset ⊕ Σ(input.amount_blinds) ⊕ …</code>  
where <tt>PSBT_GLOBAL_MWEB_TX_OFFSET</tt> supplies
<code>tx_offset</code>.  Wallets must update the global offset whenever
they add or remove commitments.

---

== Roles ==

Existing PSBT v2 roles (Creator, Constructor, Updater, Signer, Finalizer,
Extractor) are extended as follows:

* **Creator** sets the three new global fields (offsets & kernel-count) to zero or a placeholder.
* **Constructor** MUST increment <tt>MWEB_KERNEL_COUNT</tt> and update the global offsets when it appends kernel maps.
* **Signer** places Schnorr signatures into
<tt>PSBT_IN_MWEB_SIGNATURE</tt> (inputs) and
<tt>PSBT_KERNEL_SIGNATURE</tt> (kernels) and clears the appropriate
<tt>PSBT_GLOBAL_TX_MODIFIABLE</tt> bits—same logic as BIP-0370.
* **Finalizer** moves fully-signed kernel/input/output data into a canonical order, ensuring each required field for a kernel feature bit is present.
* **Extractor** serializes the transaction:
  * builds the main-chain transaction (which commits the extension block hash) from legacy PSBT data;
  * serializes the EB payload using the kernel + output information in their PSBT maps.

== Backwards Compatibility ==

* Parsers unaware of the new <keytype> values will ignore them, treating the PSBT as a “normal” v2 that happens to have unknown keys. Such tools **must not attempt to extract** a transaction.
* All new key-types are forbidden in PSBT v0.

== Reference Implementation ==

A reference implementation (Go) is provided in
<code>github.com/litecoin-project/lips/pull/###</code>, mirroring the
logic already merged into <code>ltcsuite/ltcd</code>’s PSBT package and
the Python example in <code>pylitecoin</code>.

== Rationale ==

* **Byte-values** follow the on-chain MWEB serialization as closely as possible (e.g. kernel feature bits) to minimize parsing code.  
* Separating **kernel maps** from regular output maps keeps PSBT’s tree-structure intuitive: kernels are conceptually “outputs of the block”, not of any individual input.
* Offsets belong in the *global* scope because they are transaction-wide balancing terms.

== Future Work ==

* Test vectors (binary + base64) mirroring the exhaustive list in BIP-0370 will be added once wallet implementers agree the draft.
* Optional support for **MWEB asset tags** (if activated) can be encoded via proprietary keys (<keytype> 0xFC).
